{% comment %}
  Hair-loss fit quiz. Three questions, one result screen that tells the visitor how well Elaren fits
  the KIND of hair loss they have. It never quotes a probability: the result is a band with a reason.

  Blocks:
    question  - one question (order in the sidebar = order asked)
    option    - an answer; "Belongs to question" says which question it appears under and "Points to"
                the hair-loss type it suggests (pattern / shedding / traction / medical / none)
    result    - the screen shown for one band (pattern, shedding, traction, medical)

  How the band is decided (assets/main.js, initFitQuiz):
    1. any answer pointing to "medical" wins - those visitors are told to see a doctor, not to buy;
    2. otherwise any answer pointing to "traction" wins;
    3. otherwise whichever of "pattern" / "shedding" collected more answers, pattern on a tie.
  Every result can hand the visitor to the buy box with a bundle tier pre-selected.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign questions = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'question'
  assign options = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'option'
  assign results = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'result'
  assign cta_target = section.settings.cta_link | default: '#product-section' | remove: '#'
  comment
    Placeholders are swapped inside this liquid tag: a literal "{" in an output tag trips Shopify's parser.
  endcomment
  assign current_placeholder = '{current}'
  assign total_placeholder = '{total}'
  assign step_text = section.settings.step_label | replace: current_placeholder, '1' | replace: total_placeholder, questions.size
-%}
<section class="shopify-section section" id="shopify-section-{{ section.id }}-fit-quiz">
<div class="s-fit-quiz custom-section{% if section.settings.background %} s-fit-quiz--background{% endif %}" data-fit-quiz data-section-id="{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="s-fit-quiz__container">
    <header class="s-fit-quiz__head">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}<p class="s-fit-quiz__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.title != blank -%}<h2 class="s-fit-quiz__title section-title"><p>{{ section.settings.title }}</p></h2>{%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.text != blank -%}<div class="s-fit-quiz__intro">{{ section.settings.text }}</div>{%- endif -%}
    </header>

    <div class="s-fit-quiz__card" data-quiz-card>
      {%- if questions.size > 0 -%}
      <div class="s-fit-quiz__progress" data-quiz-progress>
        <span class="s-fit-quiz__step" data-quiz-step>{{ step_text }}</span>
        <span class="s-fit-quiz__dots" aria-hidden="true">
          {%- for question in questions -%}<span class="s-fit-quiz__dot{% if forloop.first %} is-active{% endif %}"></span>{%- endfor -%}
        </span>
      </div>

      {%- for question in questions -%}
        <fieldset class="s-fit-quiz__question{% unless forloop.first %} is-hidden{% endunless %}" data-quiz-question="{{ forloop.index }}" {{ question.shopify_attributes }}>
          <legend class="s-fit-quiz__question-title">{{ question.settings.text }}</legend>
          {%- if question.settings.hint != blank -%}<p class="s-fit-quiz__question-hint">{{ question.settings.hint }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          <div class="s-fit-quiz__options">
            {%- for option in options -%}
              {%- if option.settings.question == forloop.parentloop.index -%}
              <button class="s-fit-quiz__option" type="button" data-quiz-option data-band="{{ option.settings.band }}" {{ option.shopify_attributes }}>
                <span class="s-fit-quiz__option-check" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="s-fit-quiz__option-label">{{ option.settings.label }}</span>
              </button>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </fieldset>
      {%- endfor -%}

      <div class="s-fit-quiz__nav">
        <button class="s-fit-quiz__back" type="button" data-quiz-back hidden>{{ section.settings.back_label }}</button>
      </div>
      {%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
      <p class="s-fit-quiz__empty">Add "Question" and "Answer" blocks to build the quiz.</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- for result in results -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign tier = result.settings.bundle_tier | default: 0
          assign cta_label = result.settings.cta_label
          if cta_label == blank
            assign cta_label = section.settings.cta_label
          endif
        -%}
        <div class="s-fit-quiz__result s-fit-quiz__result--{{ result.settings.band }} is-hidden" data-quiz-result="{{ result.settings.band }}" role="status" {{ result.shopify_attributes }}>
          {%- if result.settings.tag != blank -%}<span class="s-fit-quiz__result-tag">{{ result.settings.tag }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if result.settings.title != blank -%}<h3 class="s-fit-quiz__result-title">{{ result.settings.title }}</h3>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if result.settings.body != blank -%}<div class="s-fit-quiz__result-body">{{ result.settings.body }}</div>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if result.settings.expect != blank -%}
          <div class="s-fit-quiz__result-row"><span class="s-fit-quiz__result-row-label">{{ section.settings.expect_label }}</span><div class="s-fit-quiz__result-row-text">{{ result.settings.expect }}</div></div>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if result.settings.evidence != blank -%}
          <div class="s-fit-quiz__result-row"><span class="s-fit-quiz__result-row-label">{{ section.settings.evidence_label }}</span><div class="s-fit-quiz__result-row-text">{{ result.settings.evidence }}</div></div>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if result.settings.show_cta and cta_label != blank -%}
          <a class="s-fit-quiz__cta custom-button" href="#{{ cta_target }}" data-scroll-to="{{ cta_target }}" data-quiz-tier="{{ tier }}">{{ cta_label }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.restart_label != blank -%}
          <button class="s-fit-quiz__restart" type="button" data-quiz-restart>{{ section.settings.restart_label }}</button>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.footnote != blank -%}<p class="s-fit-quiz__footnote">{{ section.settings.footnote }}</p>{%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Hair-loss fit quiz",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "background", "label": "Tinted background", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "3 questions · 20 seconds" },
    { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "title", "label": "Heading", "default": "How well does Elaren fit <em>your</em> hair loss?" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "text", "label": "Intro", "default": "<p>Pumpkin seed oil and caffeine each work on a specific cause of thinning. Answer three quick questions and we’ll tell you honestly how good a match they are for yours - and when it’s better to see a doctor first.</p>" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "step_label", "label": "Progress label", "default": "Question {current} of {total}", "info": "{current} and {total} are replaced with the numbers." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "back_label", "label": "Back button", "default": "← Back" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "restart_label", "label": "Start again link", "default": "Start again" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Result screens" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "expect_label", "label": "\"What to expect\" label", "default": "What to expect" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "evidence_label", "label": "\"What the research measured\" label", "default": "What the research measured" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "See my bundle", "info": "Each result can override this." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_link", "label": "Button link", "default": "#product-section", "info": "#product-section scrolls to the buy box and pre-selects the result's bundle tier." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "footnote", "label": "Footnote", "default": "The match is based on what pumpkin seed oil and caffeine were studied for (oral pumpkin seed oil, Cho et al. 2014; topical caffeine, Dhurat et al. 2017), not on a trial of Elaren’s finished formula. It is general information, not a diagnosis. Individual results vary." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "question",
      "name": "Question",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "text", "label": "Question", "default": "Where are you noticing it most?" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "hint", "label": "Hint (optional)" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "option",
      "name": "Answer",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "range", "id": "question", "label": "Belongs to question", "min": 1, "max": 5, "step": 1, "default": 1, "info": "1 = the first Question block in the sidebar, 2 = the second, and so on." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Answer", "default": "A widening part or a thinning crown" },
        { "type": "select", "id": "band", "label": "Points to", "options": [
          { "value": "pattern", "label": "Hormonal pattern thinning (DHT)" },
          { "value": "shedding", "label": "Shedding after a trigger (telogen effluvium)" },
          { "value": "traction", "label": "Traction from tight styles" },
          { "value": "medical", "label": "See a doctor first" },
          { "value": "none", "label": "Nothing (neutral answer)" }
        ], "default": "pattern", "info": "A \"See a doctor first\" answer always decides the result, then \"Traction\", then whichever of pattern / shedding got more answers." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "result",
      "name": "Result",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "select", "id": "band", "label": "Shown for", "options": [
          { "value": "pattern", "label": "Hormonal pattern thinning (DHT)" },
          { "value": "shedding", "label": "Shedding after a trigger (telogen effluvium)" },
          { "value": "traction", "label": "Traction from tight styles" },
          { "value": "medical", "label": "See a doctor first" }
        ], "default": "pattern" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "tag", "label": "Tag", "default": "Strong match" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title", "default": "This is the kind of thinning pumpkin seed oil was studied for" },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Text", "default": "<p>A widening part, a thinning crown and receding temples that crept in gradually are the signature of hormonal pattern thinning: DHT shrinks the follicle a little more each cycle. Pumpkin seed oil’s phytosterols work on exactly that step, and the Caffeine Complex keeps the follicle in its growth phase.</p>" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "expect", "label": "What to expect", "default": "Less shedding first, usually within 2 weeks. Fuller-looking hair after 30 nights. Density that keeps building over 3–6 months, which is why the 3-month bundle is the one we recommend." },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "evidence", "label": "What the research measured", "default": "A 24-week randomised, placebo-controlled trial of pumpkin seed oil in pattern hair loss saw hair count rise 40%, four times the placebo group." },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_cta", "label": "Show the button", "default": true },
        { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "Button label override" },
        { "type": "range", "id": "bundle_tier", "label": "Pre-select bundle tier", "min": 0, "max": 5, "step": 1, "default": 2, "info": "The position of the tier in the Featured product section (1 = first card). 0 = leave the selection alone." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 30,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Hair-loss fit quiz",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "question", "settings": { "text": "Where are you noticing it most?" } },
        { "type": "option", "settings": { "question": 1, "label": "A widening part or a thinning crown", "band": "pattern" } },
        { "type": "option", "settings": { "question": 1, "label": "My temples or hairline", "band": "pattern" } },
        { "type": "option", "settings": { "question": 1, "label": "All over - more hair in the brush and the drain", "band": "shedding" } },
        { "type": "option", "settings": { "question": 1, "label": "Smooth, round bald patches", "band": "medical" } },
        { "type": "question", "settings": { "text": "When did it start?" } },
        { "type": "option", "settings": { "question": 2, "label": "Gradually, over a year or more", "band": "pattern" } },
        { "type": "option", "settings": { "question": 2, "label": "Around perimenopause or menopause", "band": "pattern" } },
        { "type": "option", "settings": { "question": 2, "label": "After a baby, an illness, surgery or a stressful stretch", "band": "shedding" } },
        { "type": "option", "settings": { "question": 2, "label": "Since wearing tight braids, extensions or ponytails", "band": "traction" } },
        { "type": "question", "settings": { "text": "How does your scalp feel?" } },
        { "type": "option", "settings": { "question": 3, "label": "Normal", "band": "none" } },
        { "type": "option", "settings": { "question": 3, "label": "Oily, flaky or dandruff-prone", "band": "none" } },
        { "type": "option", "settings": { "question": 3, "label": "Tender where my hair is pulled tight", "band": "traction" } },
        { "type": "option", "settings": { "question": 3, "label": "Itchy, sore, inflamed or scarred", "band": "medical" } },
        { "type": "result", "settings": { "band": "pattern", "tag": "Strong match", "bundle_tier": 2 } },
        { "type": "result", "settings": {
          "band": "shedding", "tag": "Likely to help", "title": "This looks like shedding after a trigger, and it usually recovers",
          "body": "<p>Hair that comes out all over a few months after a baby, an illness, surgery or a hard stretch is usually telogen effluvium: a wave of follicles resting at once. The honest news is that most of it grows back on its own over 6–12 months. Caffeine and a nightly scalp massage support the regrowth phase, and the oil helps the hair that returns come back stronger.</p>",
          "expect": "The timeline is mostly your body’s. Expect shedding to ease over the first weeks and new baby hairs along the hairline within 2–3 months. A 3-month bundle covers the recovery window.",
          "evidence": "Topical caffeine was statistically non-inferior to 5% minoxidil at increasing growth-phase hairs in a 6-month clinical study.",
          "bundle_tier": 2 } },
        { "type": "result", "settings": {
          "band": "traction", "tag": "Good match, with one condition", "title": "This is traction loss, and the style has to change first",
          "body": "<p>Thinning at the edges and temples that started with tight braids, extensions, buns or ponytails is traction alopecia. No oil regrows hair while the pulling continues. Loosen the style, give the edges a rest, and then the oil helps the recovery.</p>",
          "expect": "Once the tension is off, expect the fine hairs along the edges to return over 2–4 months. If an area has been pulled tight for years and is smooth and shiny, see a dermatologist: that can be permanent.",
          "evidence": "Pumpkin seed oil and caffeine were studied in pattern thinning, not in traction loss. Here they support regrowth that only starts when the pulling stops.",
          "bundle_tier": 1 } },
        { "type": "result", "settings": {
          "band": "medical", "tag": "See a doctor first", "title": "Please see a dermatologist before you buy anything",
          "body": "<p>Smooth round patches, or a scalp that is sore, inflamed or scarred, point to alopecia areata or a scarring alopecia. Those are medical conditions a topical oil does not address, and the earlier they are treated the better the outcome. We would rather you keep your money and get the right help.</p>",
          "expect": "Ask your GP for a referral to a dermatologist. If they rule those conditions out and find pattern thinning or shedding instead, come back: Elaren is made for those.",
          "evidence": "Pumpkin seed oil and caffeine were studied in pattern hair loss. There is no evidence for them in autoimmune or scarring hair loss, so we don’t claim any.",
          "show_cta": false, "bundle_tier": 0 } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
